# Day 2: Basic CRUD on one contact (workbook rows 7 to 12, TL steps 3 to 8)
# Send the requests in order: later ones reuse the id returned by "createContact".
# Before EVERY request: write your guessed status code in notes/day02.md, then send.
# After each request, open the contact in the HubSpot UI and look at what changed.
# Running the day again? Change @email (e.g. -2, -3) or step 7 will give 409.

@baseUrl = https://api.hubapi.com
@token = {{$dotenv HUBSPOT_TOKEN}}
@email = hslearn+d02-1@example.com
@contactId = {{createContact.response.body.id}}

### Row 7: Create one contact. Guess: 200 or 201? Save the returned id.
# @name createContact
POST {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "properties": {
    "email": "{{email}}",
    "firstname": "Test",
    "lastname": "Tester HSLearn"
  }
}

### Row 8: Read by id and ask for specific properties
# Which properties come back? Try removing ?properties=... and compare.
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts/{{contactId}}?properties=email,firstname,phone
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Row 9: Read by email instead of id
# idProperty=email tells HubSpot the path value is an email, not an id
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts/{{email}}?idProperty=email
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Row 10: Update the contact. Only the fields you send change.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts/{{contactId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "properties": {
    "firstname": "Updated",
    "phone": "+91 98765 43210"
  }
}

### Row 11: Create the same email again. Guess the code before sending!
# Read the message: where is the existing id?
POST {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "properties": {
    "email": "{{email}}"
  }
}

### Row 12: Archive the contact. Is there a response body?
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts/{{contactId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Experiment: read it again after archiving. What code now?
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts/{{contactId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stretch: list archived contacts (the recycle bin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts?archived=true&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
